{"name":"Treasure Map","hex":"#d0bb9d","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"treasure map","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A map indicating the location of buried treasure."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/treasure_map"}],"entries":[{"title":"Treasure map","blocks":[{"text":"A treasure map is a map that marks the location of buried treasure, a lost mine, a valuable secret, or a hidden locale. More common in fiction than in reality, \"pirate treasure maps\" are often depicted in works of fiction as hand drawn and containing arcane clues for the characters to follow. Regardless of the term's literary use, anything that meets the broad definition of a \"map\" that describes the location of a \"treasure\" could appropriately be called a \"treasure map.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Treasure-Island-map.jpg/330px-Treasure-Island-map.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treasure_map","wikidata":"Q1261319"},{"title":"Treasure","blocks":[{"text":"Treasure is a concentration of wealth — often originating from ancient history — that is considered lost and/or forgotten until rediscovered. Some jurisdictions legally define what constitutes treasure, such as in the British Treasure Act 1996."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg/330px-Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treasure","wikidata":"Q272937"},{"title":"Map","blocks":[{"text":"In cartography, a map is a representation or abstraction of geographic reality. Maps are used for a wide range of purposes, including navigation, scientific research, governance, and warfare. A common use is route planning, which enables users to find their way to their destination. Specialized maps called charts are used for nautical navigation and aviation. Scientists use maps to organize spatial data in fields such as geology, meteorology, seismology and demographics. Governments use maps for administrative functions such as census, electoral districts, property taxation, dispatching police, and coordinating disaster relief. Military and security organizations use maps for mission planning, surveillance, border management, logistics, and intelligence analysis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/World_Map_1689.JPG/330px-World_Map_1689.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Map","wikidata":"Q4006"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg/330px-Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg/330px-Tesoro_de_Villena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Treasure of Villena, one of the most important prehistoric golden tableware findings in Europe[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATesoro_de_Villena.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Pyle_pirates_burying2.jpg/500px-Pyle_pirates_burying2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Pyle_pirates_burying2.jpg/1280px-Pyle_pirates_burying2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Pyle_pirates_burying2.jpg/500px-Pyle_pirates_burying2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Howard Pyle's illustration of pirates burying Captain Kidd's treasure, from Howard Pyle's Book of Pirates","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APyle_pirates_burying2.jpg